<body><h1>ANSWER KEY — Set 5  <em>(grader only)</em></h1>
<p>Rubric per question: <strong>Route/action (4) · Policy stated (3) · Trap avoided (3)</strong> unless noted.</p>
<hr>
<p><strong>Q1 — Mixed / two-shipment order.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Shipping (mixed order). <strong>Action:</strong> Reassure nothing is wrong — the order ships in <strong>two separate shipments</strong>, each with its own tracking email. The first part ships shortly and the second follows. Offer to help if anything's missing after both arrive.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> treating it as a duplicate/error and cancelling or "fixing" it. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q2 — ETA, no answer yet.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> ETA / order status. <strong>Action:</strong> Empathize and apologize for the delay; tell them you're <strong>checking with the fulfillment center</strong> and will provide an update on their order within <strong>2–3 business days</strong>. Don't invent a date.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising an ETA/date that isn't confirmed. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q3 — Plain/blank item (wrong item).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Wrong item received. <strong>Action:</strong> Capelli error — request a <strong>clear evidence photo</strong> of the blank/wrong item (showing size tag) before acting; then arrange the correct item. Shopify order = FBPA. Use the quality opener.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> promising a refund/replacement with no photo. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q4 — Youth instead of adult (customer error).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Return/Exchange. <strong>Action:</strong> <strong>No exchanges</strong> — this was the customer's ordering choice. Send the return policy; they return for a refund and place a new order in the correct size.</li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> processing a size/style exchange. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q5 — Cancel (credit not applied).</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Order cancellation. <strong>Action:</strong> Confirm the details (the missing credit/coupon), confirm the order is <strong>not yet fulfilled</strong>, then cancel on the platform and process the refund. Refund posts per platform (BC 3–5 business days as "CAPELLI SPORT"). They can reorder with the credit applied.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> cancelling/refunding before verifying it isn't already fulfilled. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q6 — Size help.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Size help. <strong>Action:</strong> Point them to the <strong>size chart</strong>: click the item image, scroll to the last image in the gallery for the chart. Help them compare their child's measurements. (Store access is via the club password/app.)</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> guessing a size / promising a fit instead of directing to the chart. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q7 — Store access.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Team-store access (club-managed). <strong>Action:</strong> Store access is <strong>managed by the club</strong> — direct the customer to their coach/club administrator. <strong>Never share the club password.</strong></li><li><strong>Trap (auto-fail):</strong> sharing the club password. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q8 — Restock request.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Out of stock (replenish). <strong>Action:</strong> Tell them you've contacted the appropriate department (Planning) about replenishing the specific SKU/size, and you'll <strong>update them once it's restocked</strong>. Don't promise a firm date.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> promising a specific restock date. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q9 — Legal / complaint escalation.</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>Route:</strong> Escalation. <strong>Action:</strong> Stay calm and professional; acknowledge the specific issue (not a generic apology). <strong>Escalate</strong> to a manager; goodwill (replacement/coupon/refund) may be approved as an exception. Email only — no phone number handed out. Open + internal note.</li><li><strong>Trap:</strong> making a promise/threat-driven concession on the spot, or giving out an internal contact. <em>(4/3/3)</em></li></ul>
<p><strong>Q10 — Spot the mistake.</strong> Full credit = all <strong>three</strong> caught (≈3.3 each):</p>
<ol><li><strong>Leaks the club password</strong> ("SOCA26") — never share a club password; store access is club-managed.</li><li><strong>Promises expedited/overnight shipping</strong> — we do <strong>not</strong> offer expedited shipping.</li><li><strong>Promises arrival for the game</strong> — never promise a delivery date/event arrival.</li></ol>
<ul><li><strong>Corrected handling:</strong> direct them to their coach/club admin for store access; explain no expedited shipping and quote the standard timeline; no date promised.</li><li>Scoring: leaking the password alone = <strong>automatic fail</strong> on this question regardless of the rest. <em>(10)</em></li></ul>
<hr>
